# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# No pattern at all: classic C9 bulbs. `bulb-string` is a 32x12 tile of two
# sagging strings whose two frames trade which half of the bulbs glows; tiled
# over the whole panel it is a curtain of lights. The box is `0 0 0 0`: under
# `tile` a zero box is the whole layout, so any panel is filled edge to edge.
# No `U` line on purpose: a bigger panel gets MORE bulbs at the same 1:1 size
# rather than bigger ones. A strip wants the 1-row sprite (`strip-bulbs`):
# this one shows only the sprite's top row there — the wire, no bulbs.
S - Bulb String
L color 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Night
K 06040a
L sprite 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none tile 1
N Bulbs
I @spr/bulb-string
